efore  Jackson's nomination but the background  check should have picked up a medical  inspector general's report in 2012 that  found dr. Jackson exhibited poor  leadership in a dispute with a colleague  and as a result of the dispute overall  unit morale is at - on a scale of one to  two  one of Jackson's biggest detractors is  Montana Democratic senator Jon Tester  the ranking member of the VA committee  who insists Jackson has problems beyond  leadership as this doctor has a problem  because he hands out prescriptions like  candy in fact in the White House they  call him the Candy Man the word is is it  on overseas trips in particular that  Admiral would go down the aisle way of  the airplane and say all right who wants  to go to sleep and hand out the  prescriptions on overnight overseas  trips White House doctors do offer staff  even journalists aboard Air Force One  sleep aids I recommend that everyone on  the plane take a sleep aid at certain  times the Pentagon does the same on  trips with the Secretary of Defense but  the pills given out are recorded with  names and dosages testers candyman  comment drew a sharp response from the  White House legislative affairs director  oh it was absolutely unfair for me to  drop the can team in line I think that  there have been multiple every year they  come in and they do review of the White  House physician's office on things like  prescriptions and every year they've  said that that he's totally in  compliance with what he's been  prescribing this the White House  continues to push VA Committee Chairman  senator Johnny Isakson to reschedule  Jackson's confirmation hearing also on  Capitol Hill today Attorney General Jeff  Sessions under fire over reports his  recusal from the Russia investigation  does not extend to the investigation of  Michael Cohen are you accused from the  federal investigation of the president's  attorney Michael Cohen it is the policy  of the Department of Justice that those  who recuse themsel